event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":894,"item_id":"fc_0bb18d10865444c7016ae219ad55508191870150135f8a9ea1","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"header\":\"import Mathlib\\nopen scoped ENNReal NNReal\\nopen Set MeasureTheory\\nabbrev V (n : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)\\nnoncomputable def base {n : ℕ} (z : V (n+1)) : V n := WithLp.toLp 2 (fun i => z i.castSucc)\\ndef height {n : ℕ} (z : V (n+1)) : ℝ := z (Fin.last n)\\nnoncomputable def join {n : ℕ} (x : V n) (t : ℝ) : V (n+1) := WithLp.toLp 2 (Fin.lastCases t (fun i => x i))\\ndef unitI : Set ℝ := Set.Icc 0 1\\ndef cylinder {n : ℕ} (E : Set (V n)) : Set (V (n+1)) := {z | base z ∈ E ∧ height z ∈ unitI}\\ndef scaleCover {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) (U : ℕ → Set X) : Prop := A ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ ∀ i, Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ\\nnoncomputable def cost {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] {K : Type*} (s : ℝ) (U : K → Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ := ∑' i, (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ s\\nnoncomputable def content {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (s δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ := ⨅ (U : ℕ → Set X) (_ : scaleCover δ A U), cost s U\\nnoncomputable def haus {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (s : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ := ⨆ (δ : ℝ) (_ : 0 < δ), content s δ A\\nnoncomputable def padding {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (ε s : ℝ) (W : ℕ → Set X) (i : ℕ) : ℝ := ε * (2 : ℝ) ^ (-(i : ℝ)-1) / (1 + (Metric.diam (W i)) ^ s)\\n\",\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"n\",\"type\":\"ℕ\"},{\"name\":\"E\",\"type\":\"Set (V n)\"}],\"premise_types\":{\"H001\":\"0 ≤ n\",\"H002\":\"E.Nonempty\",\"H003\":\"IsCompact E\"},\"conclusion_type\":\"dimH (cylinder E) = dimH E + 1\",\"representation\":\"Use native EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) and encode the product directly in EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n+1)), by initial coordinates and last coordinate. No max-product metric occurs. join concatenates coordinates; the checked local squared-distance and inverse identities establish the precise Euclidean identification. Native dimH is ENNReal-valued. content and haus use positive real scales and ENNReal powers; all uses have positive exponents, so empty summands vanish. Real diameters enter only after finite-scale ediam bounds, with an explicit conversion obligation. Countable nonempty covers use a subtype of ℕ; arbitrary covers use sequences with empty padding.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[],\"terminal\":\"T027\",\"source_outputs\":{},\"endpoint_correspondence\":{\"P\":{\"mode\":\"equivalent\",\"explanation\":\"n : ℕ parametrizes exactly all nonnegative integer dimensions, with H001 retained; E is an arbitrary subset of native Euclidean ℝ^n, with precisely nonemptiness H002 and compactness H003. cylinder E consists of the vectors in Euclidean ℝ^(n+1) whose first n coordinates belong to E and whose last coordinate lies in [0,1]. The join/base/height inverse and squared-distance identities in T007 identify this set bijectively and isometrically with the stipulated Euclidean product, in both directions, including n=0. Thus native dimH of cylinder E equals the original product dimension, and dimH E + 1 is exactly D+1, with no finiteness assumption added.\"}}}}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":895,"output_index":2,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0bb18d10865444c7016ae219ad55508191870150135f8a9ea1","call_id":"call_6fb6c9e563554f69bf881dec48baaf44","name":"save_interface_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"header\":\"import Mathlib\\nopen scoped ENNReal NNReal\\nopen Set MeasureTheory\\nabbrev V (n : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)\\nnoncomputable def base {n : ℕ} (z : V (n+1)) : V n := WithLp.toLp 2 (fun i => z i.castSucc)\\ndef height {n : ℕ} (z : V (n+1)) : ℝ := z (Fin.last n)\\nnoncomputable def join {n : ℕ} (x : V n) (t : ℝ) : V (n+1) := WithLp.toLp 2 (Fin.lastCases t (fun i => x i))\\ndef unitI : Set ℝ := Set.Icc 0 1\\ndef cylinder {n : ℕ} (E : Set (V n)) : Set (V (n+1)) := {z | base z ∈ E ∧ height z ∈ unitI}\\ndef scaleCover {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) (U : ℕ → Set X) : Prop := A ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ ∀ i, Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ\\nnoncomputable def cost {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] {K : Type*} (s : ℝ) (U : K → Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ := ∑' i, (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ s\\nnoncomputable def content {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (s δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ := ⨅ (U : ℕ → Set X) (_ : scaleCover δ A U), cost s U\\nnoncomputable def haus {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (s : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ := ⨆ (δ : ℝ) (_ : 0 < δ), content s δ A\\nnoncomputable def padding {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (ε s : ℝ) (W : ℕ → Set X) (i : ℕ) : ℝ := ε * (2 : ℝ) ^ (-(i : ℝ)-1) / (1 + (Metric.diam (W i)) ^ s)\\n\",\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"n\",\"type\":\"ℕ\"},{\"name\":\"E\",\"type\":\"Set (V n)\"}],\"premise_types\":{\"H001\":\"0 ≤ n\",\"H002\":\"E.Nonempty\",\"H003\":\"IsCompact E\"},\"conclusion_type\":\"dimH (cylinder E) = dimH E + 1\",\"representation\":\"Use native EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) and encode the product directly in EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n+1)), by initial coordinates and last coordinate. No max-product metric occurs. join concatenates coordinates; the checked local squared-distance and inverse identities establish the precise Euclidean identification. Native dimH is ENNReal-valued. content and haus use positive real scales and ENNReal powers; all uses have positive exponents, so empty summands vanish. Real diameters enter only after finite-scale ediam bounds, with an explicit conversion obligation. Countable nonempty covers use a subtype of ℕ; arbitrary covers use sequences with empty padding.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[],\"terminal\":\"T027\",\"source_outputs\":{},\"endpoint_correspondence\":{\"P\":{\"mode\":\"equivalent\",\"explanation\":\"n : ℕ parametrizes exactly all nonnegative integer dimensions, with H001 retained; E is an arbitrary subset of native Euclidean ℝ^n, with precisely nonemptiness H002 and compactness H003. cylinder E consists of the vectors in Euclidean ℝ^(n+1) whose first n coordinates belong to E and whose last coordinate lies in [0,1]. The join/base/height inverse and squared-distance identities in T007 identify this set bijectively and isometrically with the stipulated Euclidean product, in both directions, including n=0. Thus native dimH of cylinder E equals the original product dimension, and dimH E + 1 is exactly D+1, with no finiteness assumption added.\"}}}}","status":"completed"}}

